From: mwlaboratories <info@mwlabs.be>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx371: enable mapped couplet correction

The IMX371 front camera of the OnePlus 6 shows a regular dot lattice
(about 8 px period) over the whole image. Its register table disables
mapped couplet correction (CCS 0x0B05, the sensor's correction of the
factory mapped pixel pairs, where the phase detection pixels sit), while
the IMX376 table, whose images show no such pattern, enables it. Enable
it for the IMX371 too.

Status: hypothesis until tested on the OnePlus 6.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c
@@ -330,7 +330,7 @@
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3617), 0x66},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x0106), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x0B00), 0x00},
-	{CCI_REG8(0x0B05), 0x00},
+	{CCI_REG8(0x0B05), 0x01},	/* mapped couplet (PDAF pixel) correction */
 	{CCI_REG8(0x0B06), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3230), 0x00},
 	{CCI_REG8(0x3602), 0x00},
